        "excerpt": "Crossplots for Porosity, Lithology and Saturation\nSchlumberger\n4-1\nCP\nThe neutron-density-sonic crossplot charts (Charts CP-1, CP-2\nand CP-7) provide insight into lithology and permit the determi-\nnation of porosity. Chart selection depends on the anticipated\nmineralogy. Neutron-density can be used to differentiate between\nthe common reservoir rocks [quartz sandstone, calcite (lime-\nstone) and dolomite] and shale and some evaporites. \nSonic-neutron can be used to differentiate between the common\nreservoir rocks when clay content is negligible. Sonic-density\ncan be used to differentiate between a single known reservoir\nrock and shale and to identify evaporate minerals.\nContinued on next page\nPorosity and Lithology Determination from\nFormation Density Log and SNP Sidewall Neutron Porosity Log\nCP-1a\n0                              10                             20\n             30                             40\nφSNPcor, neutron porosity index (p.u.) (apparent limestone porosity)\n1.9\n2.0\n2.1\n2.2\n2.3\n2.4\n2.5\n2.6\n2.7\n2.8\n2.9\n3.0\nρb, bulk density (g/cm3)\nφD, density porosity (p.u.) (ρma = 2.71, ρf = 1.0)\n45\n40\n35\n30\n25\n20\n15\n10\n5\n0\n–5\n–10\n–15\nSulfur\nSalt\nTrona\nPolyhalite\nLangbeinite\nApproxi"
